# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — NESTED comprehensions.
#
# The inner comprehension is invariant in BOTH loop variables, so the outer
# comprehension's element expression is itself a loop whose body aliases `s`.
# Before the fix the inner arm moved `s` on every inner iteration and the outer
# arm re-entered it on every outer iteration; the two inner vectors and the
# outer vector then freed one heap buffer four times.
#
# AXIS CELL: comprehension kind = LIST × LIST (nested) · body sub-position =
# ELEMENT · source = RANGE × RANGE · element type = Vector[String].
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD, both lanes: run rc 134, `free(): double free
# detected in tcache 2` (C and `--backend=llvm`); `--sanitize` reports
# `AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free`.
#
# ⚠ NOT `todo/t0003`'s nested residual (`[[c for c in w] for w in ws]`, which
# ICEs at `src/ir/lowering/mod.rs` resource-move validation before codegen).
# This cell COMPILES on both lanes at pre-fix HEAD and fails at RUN, and its
# inner body does not mention either loop variable — that invariance is the
# whole point.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Vector[Vector[String]] rows = [[s for i in 0..2] for j in 0..2]
    print(rows.len())
    print("".join(rows[0]))
    print("".join(rows[1]))
